---
// Draft ToS from a standard SaaS template (OS-293). Needs a lawyer review pass
// before launch — see the governing-law section for the one open placeholder.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 13, 2026';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'the-service', label: 'The service' },
	{ id: 'your-account', label: 'Your account' },
	{ id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
	{ id: 'payments', label: 'Payments' },
	{ id: 'your-data', label: 'Your content & data' },
	{ id: 'termination', label: 'Termination' },
	{ id: 'disclaimers', label: 'Disclaimers & limitation of liability' },
	{ id: 'governing-law', label: 'Governing law' },
	{ id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to these terms' },
	{ id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Service — OrderSail"
	description="The terms that govern use of OrderSail: accounts, acceptable use, payments through Stripe Connect, and how the beta service works."
>
	<section class="head">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
		<p class="lede">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
	</section>

	<nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections on this page">
		<ol>
			{
				sections.map((s) => (
					<li>
						<a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.label}</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ol>
	</nav>

	<article class="legal">
		<p>
			These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern access to and use of OrderSail
			("OrderSail," "we," "us"), including the dashboard, storefront, point-of-sale
			app, and API (together, the "Service"). By creating an account or using the
			Service you agree to these Terms. If you're accepting on behalf of a
			business, you're confirming you have the authority to do so.
		</p>

		<h2 id="the-service">1. The service</h2>
		<p>
			OrderSail is currently in <strong>beta</strong>. Features may change, break,
			or be removed with little notice, and we don't guarantee uptime or data
			retention during this period. We'll aim to give notice of breaking changes
			where practical.
		</p>

		<h2 id="your-account">2. Your account</h2>
		<p>
			You must provide accurate account information and are responsible for
			activity under your account, including staff you invite. You must be at
			least 18 years old, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction, to hold an
			account. Notify us promptly of any unauthorized use.
		</p>

		<h2 id="acceptable-use">3. Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>
			Use of the Service is subject to our <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable
			Use Policy</a>, which covers prohibited businesses, prohibited activities,
			and enforcement. We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate it.
		</p>

		<h2 id="payments">4. Payments</h2>
		<p>
			OrderSail uses <strong>Stripe</strong> (via Stripe Connect) to process
			payments and pay out merchants. Stripe's own terms and fees apply to
			payment processing, and Stripe — not OrderSail — holds and moves the
			funds. OrderSail doesn't add a per-transaction fee on top of Stripe's
			processing fee; see <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for subscription costs,
			if any apply.
		</p>

		<h2 id="your-data">5. Your content & data</h2>
		<p>
			You own your catalog, order, and customer data. You grant OrderSail a
			license to process it solely to provide the Service. Our handling of
			personal data is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
			A Data Processing Agreement is available for merchants who need one for
			their own compliance obligations — contact us to request it.
		</p>

		<h2 id="termination">6. Termination</h2>
		<p>
			You can close your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate an
			account for a violation of these Terms or the Acceptable Use Policy, or
			with notice for any other reason during the beta period. On termination,
			you can export your data through the API for a reasonable period
			beforehand.
		</p>

		<h2 id="disclaimers">7. Disclaimers & limitation of liability</h2>
		<p>
			The Service is provided "as is," especially during beta, without
			warranties of any kind, express or implied. To the maximum extent
			permitted by law, OrderSail isn't liable for indirect, incidental, or
			consequential damages arising from use of the Service, and our total
			liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid OrderSail in the
			twelve months before the claim arose.
		</p>

		<h2 id="governing-law">8. Governing law</h2>
		<p>
			<em
				>[Placeholder — governing law and jurisdiction to be finalized during
				legal review before launch.]</em
			>
		</p>

		<h2 id="changes">9. Changes to these terms</h2>
		<p>
			We may update these Terms as the Service changes. We'll update the "last
			updated" date above, and for material changes we'll make a reasonable
			effort to notify account owners directly.
		</p>

		<h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about these Terms can be sent through the <a href="/contact"
				>contact page</a
			>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.head {
		padding: 40px 0 32px;
	}
	.head h1 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin: 0 0 14px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.toc {
		padding: 24px 0 32px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
		margin-bottom: 40px;
	}
	.toc ol {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px 28px;
	}
	.toc a {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}
	.toc a:hover {
		color: var(--ink);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		padding-bottom: 90px;
		font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		margin: 40px 0 12px;
		scroll-margin-top: 24px;
	}
	.legal p {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
	}
	.legal a {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
</style>
